(934884, 105190, 3599, '<td valign="top">I like the movement in the sea and the warm sky.  I don''t like the border, either you added a border within the border or when you did unsharp mask it created a halo with the border.  It just looks very jagged on the right side.  Loose the border and you have a better picture (4).</td>', 'I like the movement in the sea and the warm sky.  I don''t like the border, either you added a border within the border or when you did unsharp mask it created a halo with the border.  It just looks very jagged on the right side.  Loose the border and you have a better picture (4).', '2004-10-01 15:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(934885, 108276, 20204, '<td valign="top">WOW!!!!  I can''t wait to see who did this one and where it was taken...  Absolutely goes on my favorites list.  I have nothing to critique as I would not change anything.  Great dramatic lighting, I love the surreal feel of the image, and what really captures my attention is the way you''ve isolated the detailed silhouettes of the central trees from the thicher trees to the right.</td>', 'WOW!!!!  I can''t wait to see who did this one and where it was taken...  Absolutely goes on my favorites list.  I have nothing to critique as I would not change anything.  Great dramatic lighting, I love the surreal feel of the image, and what really captures my attention is the way you''ve isolated the detailed silhouettes of the central trees from the thicher trees to the right.', '2004-10-01 15:21:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(934887, 104027, 12332, '<td valign="top">nice capture of the architect''s vision, eye stays on the subject - spelled n'' wrong (just kidding)</td>', 'nice capture of the architect''s vision, eye stays on the subject - spelled n'' wrong (just kidding)', '2004-10-01 15:21:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(934890, 107876, 3599, '<td valign="top">I really don''t like the shallow depth of field here.  Maybe just bit too extreme. Not sure if you''re going for a high-key look or it just seems a tad overexposed as well (4).</td>', 'I really don''t like the shallow depth of field here.  Maybe just bit too extreme. Not sure if you''re going for a high-key look or it just seems a tad overexposed as well (4).', '2004-10-01 15:23:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(934893, 108924, 12332, '<td valign="top">sunsets might be cliche, but I love them, and this is a great shot - brightest highlights are overexposed, but the near clouds are unique and obviously make the shot</td>', 'sunsets might be cliche, but I love them, and this is a great shot - brightest highlights are overexposed, but the near clouds are unique and obviously make the shot', '2004-10-01 15:24:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(934896, 108984, 12332, '<td valign="top">wow - making me hungry - texture, focus, highlights are excellent</td>', 'wow - making me hungry - texture, focus, highlights are excellent', '2004-10-01 15:25:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(934897, 103619, 20204, '<td valign="top">This doesn''t have much emotional appeal for me, but it''s obvious you''re creatiivity is above average and know how to make your gear work for you.  I think this would get a higher rating from me if it were set in a boxing ring setting rather than a plain white background.  That would probably make your technique more difficult, but would put the emotion back into it.  Either way, kudos for an image worth taking a second look at!</td>', 'This doesn''t have much emotional appeal for me, but it''s obvious you''re creatiivity is above average and know how to make your gear work for you.  I think this would get a higher rating from me if it were set in a boxing ring setting rather than a plain white background.  That would probably make your technique more difficult, but would put the emotion back into it.  Either way, kudos for an image worth taking a second look at!', '2004-10-01 15:26:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(934900, 107300, 3599, '<td valign="top">This picture is very nice:  The white dress, the white pillars and floor.  But the transparent white border thing is um not my style.  Other then that it does have a dreamy atmosphere so I guess using it here isn''t completely bad (6).</td>', 'This picture is very nice:  The white dress, the white pillars and floor.  But the transparent white border thing is um not my style.  Other then that it does have a dreamy atmosphere so I guess using it here isn''t completely bad (6).', '2004-10-01 15:27:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(934901, 108872, 22239, '<td valign="top">Great color contrast...  the consistency of the orange across the image is perfect... I''m very impressed if this was done with available light.  Perhaps a looser crop, or a hair less on the bottom, would balance it even better... but as is, great shot.<br/></td>', 'Great color contrast...  the consistency of the orange across the image is perfect... I''m very impressed if this was done with available light.  Perhaps a looser crop, or a hair less on the bottom, would balance it even better... but as is, great shot.', '2004-10-01 15:27:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(934905, 108949, 20204, '<td valign="top">Seems a bit dark, and there''s abit of motion blur near the tiger''s backside.  I''m sure with the darkness it would have been tough to work with a higher shutter speed.  Not sure what length lens you used, but there are relatively inexpensive attachments for speedlights that throw their beams a good distance.  If used off-camera form a remote, it would have been just what this shot needed.  I *do* like your use of space, and you obvioulsy had a solid focus on the eyes, so overall this is a great shot.</td>', 'Seems a bit dark, and there''s abit of motion blur near the tiger''s backside.  I''m sure with the darkness it would have been tough to work with a higher shutter speed.  Not sure what length lens you used, but there are relatively inexpensive attachments for speedlights that throw their beams a good distance.  If used off-camera form a remote, it would have been just what this shot needed.  I *do* like your use of space, and you obvioulsy had a solid focus on the eyes, so overall this is a great shot.', '2004-10-01 15:28:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(934907, 106707, 3599, '<td valign="top">I may be the lone person thinking this but I found that this photo is way overdone in regards to dodging and burning.  The colors are splendid and the subject and composition are nice too (5).</td>', 'I may be the lone person thinking this but I found that this photo is way overdone in regards to dodging and burning.  The colors are splendid and the subject and composition are nice too (5).', '2004-10-01 15:29:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(934908, 103105, 22239, '<td valign="top">Looks like a museum model... the soft focus and shallow DOF really make this shot, and the unseen element off to the side creates interest.  The fur detail is great.</td>', 'Looks like a museum model... the soft focus and shallow DOF really make this shot, and the unseen element off to the side creates interest.  The fur detail is great.', '2004-10-01 15:29:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(934910, 108275, 20204, '<td valign="top">The b/w treatment adds a really interesting effect to the animal''s facial expression.  Perfect catch-lights in the eyes as well.</td>', 'The b/w treatment adds a really interesting effect to the animal''s facial expression.  Perfect catch-lights in the eyes as well.', '2004-10-01 15:29:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(934911, 102742, 12332, '<td valign="top">cute idea well executed technically - I would have preferred to see more of the girl''s face, and to have her hips/legs in a more natural position - and the paint can looks adult-prepared</td>', 'cute idea well executed technically - I would have preferred to see more of the girl''s face, and to have her hips/legs in a more natural position - and the paint can looks adult-prepared', '2004-10-01 15:30:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(934913, 107586, 24076, '<td valign="top">I don''t understand the title, but it''s a great shot!</td>', 'I don''t understand the title, but it''s a great shot!', '2004-10-01 15:30:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(934916, 106953, 3080, '<td valign="top">Very nice focus and clarity.  I love the crispness.  I wish she didn''t look so sad.  I think her eyes are competing with the tree bright dots to the right of her face.  In other words, i find the dots to be a distraction from her face.  They are so close to her face, and similar to size and color to her eyes, that my eyes are drawn over to the dots as well as her eyes.  Still a very lovely photo and beautiful girl as well. ~Heather~</td>', 'Very nice focus and clarity.  I love the crispness.  I wish she didn''t look so sad.  I think her eyes are competing with the tree bright dots to the right of her face.  In other words, i find the dots to be a distraction from her face.  They are so close to her face, and similar to size and color to her eyes, that my eyes are drawn over to the dots as well as her eyes.  Still a very lovely photo and beautiful girl as well. ~Heather~', '2004-10-01 15:31:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(934920, 102742, 20204, '<td valign="top">Very creative!  This shot is technically great, and it''s great to see selective desat used with style and skill.  I bet you''d do well with this on DPC Prints.  There''s a great feel of balance to this shot.</td>', 'Very creative!  This shot is technically great, and it''s great to see selective desat used with style and skill.  I bet you''d do well with this on DPC Prints.  There''s a great feel of balance to this shot.', '2004-10-01 15:31:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(934922, 108569, 12332, '<td valign="top">focus makes it appear slightly impressionistic, but then it lacks the color to pull that off</td>', 'focus makes it appear slightly impressionistic, but then it lacks the color to pull that off', '2004-10-01 15:31:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(934923, 107091, 22239, '<td valign="top">I like the use of negative space here, though the sloped ground seems to throw things off a little bit, as it fools with my sense of horizon.  As a result, the people appear to be leaning a bit unnaturally.  Also, I would have liked to see either a more intentional silhouette approach with less detail on the people, or a bit more exposure on them to bring out some of the variation.  Right now, the foreground elements get caught between the extremes of silhouette and enough exposure to see detail.</td>', 'I like the use of negative space here, though the sloped ground seems to throw things off a little bit, as it fools with my sense of horizon.  As a result, the people appear to be leaning a bit unnaturally.  Also, I would have liked to see either a more intentional silhouette approach with less detail on the people, or a bit more exposure on them to bring out some of the variation.  Right now, the foreground elements get caught between the extremes of silhouette and enough exposure to see detail.', '2004-10-01 15:31:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(934925, 107969, 26464, '<td valign="top">just awesome<br/></td>', 'just awesome', '2004-10-01 15:32:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(934926, 105966, 20204, '<td valign="top">Very dramatic, and what great colors - smooth like butter.  I''m feeling like the cropping is a bit tight in the upper left corner, but overall, what a great image!</td>', 'Very dramatic, and what great colors - smooth like butter.  I''m feeling like the cropping is a bit tight in the upper left corner, but overall, what a great image!', '2004-10-01 15:32:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(934927, 107995, 26464, '<td valign="top">great idea, could itself be in a magazine.. you should send it in to it for consideration<br/></td>', 'great idea, could itself be in a magazine.. you should send it in to it for consideration', '2004-10-01 15:32:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(934930, 103219, 26464, '<td valign="top">very soft and pleasing to the eye. <br/></td>', 'very soft and pleasing to the eye. ', '2004-10-01 15:33:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(934931, 105984, 12332, '<td valign="top">I would have liked a little more DOF, to keep the antennae and legs in focus, but not a major problem</td>', 'I would have liked a little more DOF, to keep the antennae and legs in focus, but not a major problem', '2004-10-01 15:33:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(934934, 103619, 3080, '<td valign="top">Even though I have had a bit of insight on how this was done, I''m still not sure if I prefer the results.  It is very clever.  Points for that.  I guess it''s just not my thing.  I''m not ''into'' it.  Technically, it''s very well done.  Good focus, lighting and nothing distracting in the background.  ~Heather~</td>', 'Even though I have had a bit of insight on how this was done, I''m still not sure if I prefer the results.  It is very clever.  Points for that.  I guess it''s just not my thing.  I''m not ''into'' it.  Technically, it''s very well done.  Good focus, lighting and nothing distracting in the background.  ~Heather~', '2004-10-01 15:34:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(934935, 107202, 20204, '<td valign="top">Not really my style of art, but I can respect the skill it took to make this image.</td>', 'Not really my style of art, but I can respect the skill it took to make this image.', '2004-10-01 15:34:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(934937, 107876, 24076, '<td valign="top">I think a black background would have served up this beauty better than the white.</td>', 'I think a black background would have served up this beauty better than the white.', '2004-10-01 15:35:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(934940, 107609, 20204, '<td valign="top">The longer I look at this image the more interesting it becomes...  The highlights are a bit harsh, but it''s a very compelling shot for its emotional appeal.  Great work!</td>', 'The longer I look at this image the more interesting it becomes...  The highlights are a bit harsh, but it''s a very compelling shot for its emotional appeal.  Great work!', '2004-10-01 15:36:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(934942, 108995, 3599, '<td valign="top">Looks like a picture that I would see in the liner notes for a CD.  I don''t like the technique used to make it look like regular film.  It doesn''t work for me because it is too uniform and looks like it was intentially applied (4).</td>', 'Looks like a picture that I would see in the liner notes for a CD.  I don''t like the technique used to make it look like regular film.  It doesn''t work for me because it is too uniform and looks like it was intentially applied (4).', '2004-10-01 15:36:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(934943, 109032, 22239, '<td valign="top">Great approach to get the "opponent," as well as a unique (though, difficult to perceive at first) viewpoint on the action... reminds me of the video game "Punch Out."  Unfortunately, the result upon first glance is a strange out-of-focus effect on most of the body of your boxer, which throws off my eye in the scene.  The lighting is good, but the composition seems a little cramped.  The image looks either over-smoothed (NeatImage?) or slightly out of focus on the boxer, so there''s little detail on her face... perhaps a fill light would have helped get a little more of the expression on her face.</td>', 'Great approach to get the "opponent," as well as a unique (though, difficult to perceive at first) viewpoint on the action... reminds me of the video game "Punch Out."  Unfortunately, the result upon first glance is a strange out-of-focus effect on most of the body of your boxer, which throws off my eye in the scene.  The lighting is good, but the composition seems a little cramped.  The image looks either over-smoothed (NeatImage?) or slightly out of focus on the boxer, so there''s little detail on her face... perhaps a fill light would have helped get a little more of the expression on her face.', '2004-10-01 15:36:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(934944, 108995, 26464, '<td valign="top">i dont know, i just dont think the grain here works.<br/>maybe more contrast?<br/></td>', 'i dont know, i just dont think the grain here works.maybe more contrast?', '2004-10-01 15:37:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(934945, 105984, 3080, '<td valign="top">I wish the whole butterfly was in focus.  probably a difficult task to ask for, but with the upper wings out of focus, it almost makes it look like a bad editing job, where you blurred the background and oops, must have gotten the upper wing accidently.  I know this is probably not the case, but my first impression when I see it.  Focus on the rest of the bfly is nice.  lighting is good, and background contains no distracting elements.  Overall nice, but not extraordinary. ~Heather~</td>', 'I wish the whole butterfly was in focus.  probably a difficult task to ask for, but with the upper wings out of focus, it almost makes it look like a bad editing job, where you blurred the background and oops, must have gotten the upper wing accidently.  I know this is probably not the case, but my first impression when I see it.  Focus on the rest of the bfly is nice.  lighting is good, and background contains no distracting elements.  Overall nice, but not extraordinary. ~Heather~', '2004-10-01 15:37:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(934946, 107202, 26464, '<td valign="top">errr... <br/></td>', 'errr... ', '2004-10-01 15:37:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(934948, 108210, 12332, '<td valign="top">pretty colors - potential jigsaw puzzle - I would like it even better with the bottom 20% and right 20% cropped out, I think - or if you moved to the right and kept the tall trees, blocked the lower house a little, and got the whole height of the lighthouse</td>', 'pretty colors - potential jigsaw puzzle - I would like it even better with the bottom 20% and right 20% cropped out, I think - or if you moved to the right and kept the tall trees, blocked the lower house a little, and got the whole height of the lighthouse', '2004-10-01 15:37:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(934949, 104027, 20204, '<td valign="top">Great architectural image!  I''m very curious how this would look in b/w as it might emphasize the shapes / lines and blend the foreground more with the background.  Not my choice to make, and not necessary for enjoyment of this image - you''ve done a great job (but I''m still curious!)</td>', 'Great architectural image!  I''m very curious how this would look in b/w as it might emphasize the shapes / lines and blend the foreground more with the background.  Not my choice to make, and not necessary for enjoyment of this image - you''ve done a great job (but I''m still curious!)', '2004-10-01 15:38:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(934951, 103619, 26464, '<td valign="top">awesome concept and execution. <br/></td>', 'awesome concept and execution. ', '2004-10-01 15:38:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(934952, 108897, 3599, '<td valign="top">Very nice studio shot.  Nice lighting and pose.  I may cropped a little off the bottom and sides (6).</td>', 'Very nice studio shot.  Nice lighting and pose.  I may cropped a little off the bottom and sides (6).', '2004-10-01 15:39:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(934953, 103788, 12332, '<td valign="top">Yes! great geometry, texture, detail, and shadows - hope you put this up for sale</td>', 'Yes! great geometry, texture, detail, and shadows - hope you put this up for sale', '2004-10-01 15:39:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(934954, 108949, 3080, '<td valign="top">Who am I to tell a "master" anything, but the colors here seem pretty dull.  I took it into the AOL edit photo and hit auto enhance and it made a WORLD of difference.  Made the whites whiter and the orange stand out so much more.  I guess it just seems dark as is.  Focus seems ok and the environment looks good with the tiger.  Nothing distracting. ~Heather~</td>', 'Who am I to tell a "master" anything, but the colors here seem pretty dull.  I took it into the AOL edit photo and hit auto enhance and it made a WORLD of difference.  Made the whites whiter and the orange stand out so much more.  I guess it just seems dark as is.  Focus seems ok and the environment looks good with the tiger.  Nothing distracting. ~Heather~', '2004-10-01 15:39:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(934957, 107586, 20204, '<td valign="top">This is right out of National Geographic.  You''ve captured the image perfectly from a technical perspective, and created strong emotinal appeal.  *Outstanding* image!</td>', 'This is right out of National Geographic.  You''ve captured the image perfectly from a technical perspective, and created strong emotinal appeal.  *Outstanding* image!', '2004-10-01 15:40:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(934958, 107586, 22239, '<td valign="top">Exposure and lighting are impeccable.  Sharp detail on the skin gives a slightly gritty appearance to the image, which works well with the subject to convey an atmosphere.  It''s hard to tell what the emotion is, but it could be anything from despair to hope, which is impressive.  The hand in the foreground is a little distracting, but I''m unsure whether it would have worked any better with deeper DOF... perhaps a tighter crop if it was candid, or moving the hand if it was posed?</td>', 'Exposure and lighting are impeccable.  Sharp detail on the skin gives a slightly gritty appearance to the image, which works well with the subject to convey an atmosphere.  It''s hard to tell what the emotion is, but it could be anything from despair to hope, which is impressive.  The hand in the foreground is a little distracting, but I''m unsure whether it would have worked any better with deeper DOF... perhaps a tighter crop if it was candid, or moving the hand if it was posed?', '2004-10-01 15:40:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(934960, 106488, 3599, '<td valign="top">Really cool.  Is this infrared?  At first I thought it was snow.  Really nicely done (9).</td>', 'Really cool.  Is this infrared?  At first I thought it was snow.  Really nicely done (9).', '2004-10-01 15:41:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(934963, 107609, 3080, '<td valign="top">While I like the lighting, there are a couple shadows that I wish weren''t there, and I supose you can''t have both. lol.  The shadow from his collar is so very sharp that it draws my attention greatly.  And I wish I could see his eyes.  He''s a lovely old man.  Much personality in his face and lines.  It makes me smile. ~Heather~</td>', 'While I like the lighting, there are a couple shadows that I wish weren''t there, and I supose you can''t have both. lol.  The shadow from his collar is so very sharp that it draws my attention greatly.  And I wish I could see his eyes.  He''s a lovely old man.  Much personality in his face and lines.  It makes me smile. ~Heather~', '2004-10-01 15:42:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(934965, 104134, 22239, '<td valign="top">Good portrait.  Lighting looks natural and smooth, and brings out the detail in her hair and face without overdoing it and forcing her pupils down to pinpricks.</td>', 'Good portrait.  Lighting looks natural and smooth, and brings out the detail in her hair and face without overdoing it and forcing her pupils down to pinpricks.', '2004-10-01 15:42:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(934966, 107876, 20204, '<td valign="top">I think the key may have gone a bit too high... Looks like it''s dancing on the edge of texture loss near where the DOF cuts off on the right.  The off-center placement of the overall shape (not the strawberry) feels a bit awkward and out of balance.</td>', 'I think the key may have gone a bit too high... Looks like it''s dancing on the edge of texture loss near where the DOF cuts off on the right.  The off-center placement of the overall shape (not the strawberry) feels a bit awkward and out of balance.', '2004-10-01 15:42:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(934967, 105966, 3599, '<td valign="top">This is really cool.  Just enough light to illuminate part of the balloon with the silouhettes of other balloons on the sky make this a great shot (8).</td>', 'This is really cool.  Just enough light to illuminate part of the balloon with the silouhettes of other balloons on the sky make this a great shot (8).', '2004-10-01 15:43:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(934969, 107202, 12332, '<td valign="top">well executed, but not very politically correct (no deduct) - would have preferred to see what was between her other cheeks (ie, face)</td>', 'well executed, but not very politically correct (no deduct) - would have preferred to see what was between her other cheeks (ie, face)', '2004-10-01 15:44:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(934970, 108984, 22239, '<td valign="top">Great interpretation on the classic RGB theme.  The curves on the pepper are luxurious.  There seems to be a bit of a lighting halo around the pepper and off in the lower left which seems to disturb the consistency of the blue backdrop.  The brownish bit on the end of the stem is a bit distracting as well... perhaps trimming it a bit would have made the green seem even more pure.  Great lighting and color saturation.</td>', 'Great interpretation on the classic RGB theme.  The curves on the pepper are luxurious.  There seems to be a bit of a lighting halo around the pepper and off in the lower left which seems to disturb the consistency of the blue backdrop.  The brownish bit on the end of the stem is a bit distracting as well... perhaps trimming it a bit would have made the green seem even more pure.  Great lighting and color saturation.', '2004-10-01 15:44:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(934973, 109014, 12332, '<td valign="top">needed just a bit more DOF, but a great shot just the same</td>', 'needed just a bit more DOF, but a great shot just the same', '2004-10-01 15:44:57.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(934975, 107091, 20204, '<td valign="top">I''m curious to see if you get comments on having too much sky.  I like it, and commend you for subtle rule-breaking.  The composition creates a feeling of the glider pilot''s feel as he heads for the wide open sky, as opposed to focusing on the tethers to earth.  This is a great image!</td>', 'I''m curious to see if you get comments on having too much sky.  I like it, and commend you for subtle rule-breaking.  The composition creates a feeling of the glider pilot''s feel as he heads for the wide open sky, as opposed to focusing on the tethers to earth.  This is a great image!', '2004-10-01 15:45:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(934977, 107488, 200, '<td valign="top">of all of the wonderful images in this challenge...this one happens to touch me the most. Thank you :)</td>', 'of all of the wonderful images in this challenge...this one happens to touch me the most. Thank you :)', '2004-10-01 15:45:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(934978, 108269, 3080, '<td valign="top">While I''m sure it was a magnificent sight to see, I don''t think the camera was able to capture it how you must have saw it.  The colors seem dull.  Dead looking grass, blown out sunrays, and dark green water.  I think had there been more of a reflection in the water from the sun, maybe it would have been different.  But then again, who am I to question the masters. ?   It''s not like I have produced anything better.  ~Heather~</td>', 'While I''m sure it was a magnificent sight to see, I don''t think the camera was able to capture it how you must have saw it.  The colors seem dull.  Dead looking grass, blown out sunrays, and dark green water.  I think had there been more of a reflection in the water from the sun, maybe it would have been different.  But then again, who am I to question the masters. ?   It''s not like I have produced anything better.  ~Heather~', '2004-10-01 15:46:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(934980, 107902, 20204, '<td valign="top">I''d love to see this in sepia...  Might help it to feel less busy.  Very interesting scene.  Would be great if the window wasn''t cut off (top ctr.) as well.</td>', 'I''d love to see this in sepia...  Might help it to feel less busy.  Very interesting scene.  Would be great if the window wasn''t cut off (top ctr.) as well.', '2004-10-01 15:47:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(934981, 107876, 12332, '<td valign="top">irresistable - captures the lightness of the food, could have used a little more DOF - makes me sad to be on the Atkins right now</td>', 'irresistable - captures the lightness of the food, could have used a little more DOF - makes me sad to be on the Atkins right now', '2004-10-01 15:47:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(934982, 107901, 22239, '<td valign="top">Wonderful colors in this... clear sky blue contrasts well with the vivid red of the dragonfly, and the flower balances it off with the rest of the spectrum.  The DOF on this seems too shallow... the tips of the foreground petals, the far wings and tail on the dragonfly, and the far leaves on the flower are a bit too blurry for my tastes.  If this shot were from head-on, the shallow DOF would emphasize the insect''s face, but as taken, this DOF choice fails to pull my attention to a specific subject.</td>', 'Wonderful colors in this... clear sky blue contrasts well with the vivid red of the dragonfly, and the flower balances it off with the rest of the spectrum.  The DOF on this seems too shallow... the tips of the foreground petals, the far wings and tail on the dragonfly, and the far leaves on the flower are a bit too blurry for my tastes.  If this shot were from head-on, the shallow DOF would emphasize the insect''s face, but as taken, this DOF choice fails to pull my attention to a specific subject.', '2004-10-01 15:47:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(934984, 108843, 3599, '<td valign="top">Everytime I see this rock I can''t help but think of Goonies.  Everything about this photo is great (10).</td>', 'Everytime I see this rock I can''t help but think of Goonies.  Everything about this photo is great (10).', '2004-10-01 15:47:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(934988, 103105, 15207, '<td valign="top">I absolutely love this. The lighting is perfect. Plus, I have an addiction to spider monkeys - tried to shoot wild ones in Costa Rica and the majority didn''t turn out b/c of bad sunlight. The only thing that would make this a perfect 10 is if the feet and hands were showing. However, the emotion and drama is definitely caputred regardless.</td>', 'I absolutely love this. The lighting is perfect. Plus, I have an addiction to spider monkeys - tried to shoot wild ones in Costa Rica and the majority didn''t turn out b/c of bad sunlight. The only thing that would make this a perfect 10 is if the feet and hands were showing. However, the emotion and drama is definitely caputred regardless.', '2004-10-01 15:48:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(934989, 103788, 20204, '<td valign="top">This is one of VERY few 10s I''ve ever given out.  The elements and perspective are very unique, use of b/w emphasizes the lines beautifully and the contrast between the soft lines of the sky and the sharp rigging of the boat create a perfect image.  I hope you put this on DPC prints and it brings you success.</td>', 'This is one of VERY few 10s I''ve ever given out.  The elements and perspective are very unique, use of b/w emphasizes the lines beautifully and the contrast between the soft lines of the sky and the sharp rigging of the boat create a perfect image.  I hope you put this on DPC prints and it brings you success.', '2004-10-01 15:48:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(934992, 108454, 22239, '<td valign="top">Beautiful sky and incredible natural formations... the size difference between the totems effectively enforces a partial sense of depth even with a deep DOF.  The saturation on the rocks and plant life could have used a bit of a boost to balance the jewel-like blue of the sky.</td>', 'Beautiful sky and incredible natural formations... the size difference between the totems effectively enforces a partial sense of depth even with a deep DOF.  The saturation on the rocks and plant life could have used a bit of a boost to balance the jewel-like blue of the sky.', '2004-10-01 15:49:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(934993, 107969, 12332, '<td valign="top">stylistic rendering is appealling, composition keeps my eyes in the photo</td>', 'stylistic rendering is appealling, composition keeps my eyes in the photo', '2004-10-01 15:49:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(934994, 108875, 20204, '<td valign="top">I''d like to see a bit more sharpness &amp; emphasis on the foreground - perhaps by shooting from a lower point of view...  Just enough to have it lead your eye outward rather than be skipped over entirely.</td>', 'I''d like to see a bit more sharpness & emphasis on the foreground - perhaps by shooting from a lower point of view...  Just enough to have it lead your eye outward rather than be skipped over entirely.', '2004-10-01 15:50:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(934998, 102660, 20204, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure what to make of the expression.  A beautiful model, and I like the lighting &amp; color treatment very much.  There''s just something about the expression that isn''t fitting in for me.</td>', 'I''m not sure what to make of the expression.  A beautiful model, and I like the lighting & color treatment very much.  There''s just something about the expression that isn''t fitting in for me.', '2004-10-01 15:51:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(934999, 108940, 12332, '<td valign="top">nice capture of softness and textures. would have liked to see pistel/stamen in better focus (might be due to bringing photo to competition size)</td>', 'nice capture of softness and textures. would have liked to see pistel/stamen in better focus (might be due to bringing photo to competition size)', '2004-10-01 15:51:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(935000, 106707, 15207, '<td valign="top">I can''t wait to read how you did this. I''ve never seen such beautiful depth in a sunset photo. Your technique with ap. and shutter speed, etc. is pitch perfect, and so is this image. I''m betting on the blue ribbon.</td>', 'I can''t wait to read how you did this. I''ve never seen such beautiful depth in a sunset photo. Your technique with ap. and shutter speed, etc. is pitch perfect, and so is this image. I''m betting on the blue ribbon.', '2004-10-01 15:53:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(935001, 109014, 20204, '<td valign="top">I''ve been working on building up my birds file lately, and still don''t have anything this nice.  Could be right out of a field guide - excellent job!</td>', 'I''ve been working on building up my birds file lately, and still don''t have anything this nice.  Could be right out of a field guide - excellent job!', '2004-10-01 15:53:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(935002, 108072, 12332, '<td valign="top">nice portrait, tough to expose, got a couple of blow-outs on the shirt but the horse would have been too dark right?</td>', 'nice portrait, tough to expose, got a couple of blow-outs on the shirt but the horse would have been too dark right?', '2004-10-01 15:53:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(935003, 108537, 22239, '<td valign="top">Soft focus, costuming, lighting, and color tone work together wonderfully here to convey period.  The contrast effectively pulls attention directly to your model''s eyes, which follows on to take in her whole mischievious expression.  Soft skin tones, good exposure, and compositional balance have me wondering what exactly she''s looking at.  My only issue lies with the chain... it seems a little heavy and anachronistic.</td>', 'Soft focus, costuming, lighting, and color tone work together wonderfully here to convey period.  The contrast effectively pulls attention directly to your model''s eyes, which follows on to take in her whole mischievious expression.  Soft skin tones, good exposure, and compositional balance have me wondering what exactly she''s looking at.  My only issue lies with the chain... it seems a little heavy and anachronistic.', '2004-10-01 15:53:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(935005, 108767, 20204, '<td valign="top">I think you could have gone with a standard aspect ratio on this...  The sky isn''t dramatic on the top 1/3, but there is much mystery and detail in the lower 2/3.</td>', 'I think you could have gone with a standard aspect ratio on this...  The sky isn''t dramatic on the top 1/3, but there is much mystery and detail in the lower 2/3.', '2004-10-01 15:54:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(935006, 108269, 12332, '<td valign="top">beautiful sight - waves slightly overexposed - nice colors</td>', 'beautiful sight - waves slightly overexposed - nice colors', '2004-10-01 15:55:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(935007, 103105, 4008, '<td valign="top">One of the most beautiful images with monkey''s I have ever seen. The golden glow on the fur, the position, the expressions, the background, it all fits very well together and expresses a great tenderness and caring atmosphere. I would have liked to see a bit more light in the mothers face, but realise you can''t have it all, it is not all under your control and you have to catch the moment.</td>', 'One of the most beautiful images with monkey''s I have ever seen. The golden glow on the fur, the position, the expressions, the background, it all fits very well together and expresses a great tenderness and caring atmosphere. I would have liked to see a bit more light in the mothers face, but realise you can''t have it all, it is not all under your control and you have to catch the moment.', '2004-10-01 15:56:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(935008, 107969, 20204, '<td valign="top">Looks like a bit of an unatural halo on the kiwi, but perhaps it''s backlighting.  Either way this is extremely creative, and was no doubt tricky to get "just right".  Great job!</td>', 'Looks like a bit of an unatural halo on the kiwi, but perhaps it''s backlighting.  Either way this is extremely creative, and was no doubt tricky to get "just right".  Great job!', '2004-10-01 15:56:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(935010, 106707, 12332, '<td valign="top">nice shot - potential postcard! well-exposed and crazy-wide color gamut</td>', 'nice shot - potential postcard! well-exposed and crazy-wide color gamut', '2004-10-01 15:57:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(935011, 108949, 22239, '<td valign="top">Awesome exposure and subject... the big cat''s pose and intent expression are simply majestic.  The bamboo background works well as it goes from focused and sharp to faded, dark, and shadowy, with good shadow detail.  The colors throw me off a bit, though... it seems like you might have worked with the saturation a lot.  As a result, the pole in the foreground looks splotchy, and there are cyan color artifacts on the tiger''s light fur.</td>', 'Awesome exposure and subject... the big cat''s pose and intent expression are simply majestic.  The bamboo background works well as it goes from focused and sharp to faded, dark, and shadowy, with good shadow detail.  The colors throw me off a bit, though... it seems like you might have worked with the saturation a lot.  As a result, the pole in the foreground looks splotchy, and there are cyan color artifacts on the tiger''s light fur.', '2004-10-01 15:57:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(935012, 109019, 772, '<td valign="top">Lovely image... the pose and capture of her intense gaze at the bubble is quite intriging :)  Capturing kids doing their own things, unprompted, usually results in great images :)</td>', 'Lovely image... the pose and capture of her intense gaze at the bubble is quite intriging :)  Capturing kids doing their own things, unprompted, usually results in great images :)', '2004-10-01 15:58:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(935013, 106488, 20204, '<td valign="top">Is Ansel Adams back from the dead?  Feels like a slight tilt counterclockwise, but I love this image.  Great work!</td>', 'Is Ansel Adams back from the dead?  Feels like a slight tilt counterclockwise, but I love this image.  Great work!', '2004-10-01 15:58:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(935014, 108843, 7263, '<td valign="top">This is my pick for the winner  - however for me it isn''t all that special (I can hear the gasps now). I do like the blue that has been captured / enhanced and the cloud formation is very nice too.<br/> <br/>but I can''t help but feel if a ''better'' photographer had been here they would have captured something so much more interesting.<br/> <br/>There is no foreground interest what-so-ever and likewise no middle and apart from a small rock or two no background either.<br/> <br/>It solely relies on blue and clouds which whilst looks nice for a few seconds - it doesn''t go beyond that.<br/> <br/>Composition is a little let down - there are some interesting patterns being made and reflections too on the flooring - and I feel perhaps giving 2/3 of the scene to this would have been better. Generally it is said not to place the horizon in the middle, and this is when that rule works.<br/> <br/>Another area which looks interesting is the rocks - they are large and looming with some nice ocean spray coming off of them - but you have made them so small they look like small rocks and hardly figure in the photo.<br/> <br/>I am being overly harsh here, because I feel this is good - but some scenes are so that one can''t help but shoot anywhere and get a fairly decent photo. And considering where you were and at what time - a bit of a waste.<br/></td>', 'This is my pick for the winner  - however for me it isn''t all that special (I can hear the gasps now). I do like the blue that has been captured / enhanced and the cloud formation is very nice too. but I can''t help but feel if a ''better'' photographer had been here they would have captured something so much more interesting. There is no foreground interest what-so-ever and likewise no middle and apart from a small rock or two no background either. It solely relies on blue and clouds which whilst looks nice for a few seconds - it doesn''t go beyond that. Composition is a little let down - there are some interesting patterns being made and reflections too on the flooring - and I feel perhaps giving 2/3 of the scene to this would have been better. Generally it is said not to place the horizon in the middle, and this is when that rule works. Another area which looks interesting is the rocks - they are large and looming with some nice ocean spray coming off of them - but you have made them so small they look like small rocks and hardly figure in the photo. I am being overly harsh here, because I feel this is good - but some scenes are so that one can''t help but shoot anywhere and get a fairly decent photo. And considering where you were and at what time - a bit of a waste.', '2004-10-01 15:59:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(935015, 108986, 12332, '<td valign="top">captivating focus on the eyes</td>', 'captivating focus on the eyes', '2004-10-01 15:59:25.000000', NULL, 1),
