(950036, 105190, 7263, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kiwiness:</b></div><hr/><i> Way to go Jon! A 7.9 and no blue ribbon, never seen that before :) One day you will get that elusive blue Jon, one day :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I have been telling myself that for a year now lol. I kind of like it this way. Keeps me interested ;D<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by kiwiness: Way to go Jon! A 7.9 and no blue ribbon, never seen that before :) One day you will get that elusive blue Jon, one day :)   I have been telling myself that for a year now lol. I kind of like it this way. Keeps me interested ;D', '2004-10-08 06:37:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(950037, 106707, 9913, '<td valign="top">Man this is probably one of the most overrated photos on DPC.</td>', 'Man this is probably one of the most overrated photos on DPC.', '2004-10-08 06:38:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(950038, 108276, 2798, '<td valign="top">This was one of three 10s I gave in this challenge (that''s 3 more than I usually give - the standards were VERY high here). I absolutely love the mood and the light in this picture. It captures autumn just perfectly for me and has the added bonus of looking a bit like a Weston image (with colour). Well done - I believe this deserved a ribbon.</td>', 'This was one of three 10s I gave in this challenge (that''s 3 more than I usually give - the standards were VERY high here). I absolutely love the mood and the light in this picture. It captures autumn just perfectly for me and has the added bonus of looking a bit like a Weston image (with colour). Well done - I believe this deserved a ribbon.', '2004-10-08 06:38:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(950039, 108995, 2798, '<td valign="top">OMG - how can THIS come last? This was one of my favourites and I gave it a 9. For me this image captured something about what it''s like to be at a concert. The grain gives the feel of a smoky atmosphere and the strong light and contrast really evokes the concert mood. Well done on a fantastic shot and shame on the voters for not appreciating it.</td>', 'OMG - how can THIS come last? This was one of my favourites and I gave it a 9. For me this image captured something about what it''s like to be at a concert. The grain gives the feel of a smoky atmosphere and the strong light and contrast really evokes the concert mood. Well done on a fantastic shot and shame on the voters for not appreciating it.', '2004-10-08 06:43:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(950041, 108875, 14603, '<td valign="top">Ed, thanks for the kind words, I have actually put more work into this shot than any other that I`ve submitted.(Both prior to and after taking the shot)<br/>I`m not at all bothered by my finishing place..as I said in my write up..I didn`t expect to finish anywhere near the top.<br/>However, I am delighted that far more people than I expected,took time to look at the pic and appreciate what I was trying to achieve.<br/>Because of the geography of the place and the restrictions I couldn`t include paths or features which would lead you into the pic..so I hunted for a bit foreground that would echo the shape of the undulating mountains in the backgound and went for a horizontal "thirds" split.<br/>I also wanted to keep tones exactly as I saw them..which meant a lot of manipulation to darken some areas and lighten others.<br/>The only part I was unhappy with was the foreground which was naturally underexposed and therefore aquired a graininess when I restored it to a "real life" setting. However, I felt it was important to have the foreground brighter with tone and detail getting dimmer as it receded.The result is as near to what I saw as I could have achieved.<br/>To the people who wanted a person or boat or were looking for a bit more saturation...my apologies, I can understand that these are personal preferences but they would have ruined the feel of what I was trying to create in my minds eye but I very much appreciate the input from all.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-08 12:35:33.</i></td>', 'Ed, thanks for the kind words, I have actually put more work into this shot than any other that I`ve submitted.(Both prior to and after taking the shot)I`m not at all bothered by my finishing place..as I said in my write up..I didn`t expect to finish anywhere near the top.However, I am delighted that far more people than I expected,took time to look at the pic and appreciate what I was trying to achieve.Because of the geography of the place and the restrictions I couldn`t include paths or features which would lead you into the pic..so I hunted for a bit foreground that would echo the shape of the undulating mountains in the backgound and went for a horizontal "thirds" split.I also wanted to keep tones exactly as I saw them..which meant a lot of manipulation to darken some areas and lighten others.The only part I was unhappy with was the foreground which was naturally underexposed and therefore aquired a graininess when I restored it to a "real life" setting. However, I felt it was important to have the foreground brighter with tone and detail getting dimmer as it receded.The result is as near to what I saw as I could have achieved.To the people who wanted a person or boat or were looking for a bit more saturation...my apologies, I can understand that these are personal preferences but they would have ruined the feel of what I was trying to create in my minds eye but I very much appreciate the input from all.', '2004-10-08 06:48:02.000000', '2004-10-08 13:35:33.000000', 0),
(950042, 107995, 2798, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully cleaver arrangement of the shot. Just a shame you didn''t have a studio background to shoot it in. Well done.</td>', 'Wonderfully cleaver arrangement of the shot. Just a shame you didn''t have a studio background to shoot it in. Well done.', '2004-10-08 06:48:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(950043, 106707, 8522, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nazgul:</b></div><hr/><i> Man this is probably one of the most overrated photos on DPC. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Don''t hold back, eh? LOL</td>', 'Originally posted by Nazgul: Man this is probably one of the most overrated photos on DPC.   Don''t hold back, eh? LOL', '2004-10-08 06:53:48.000000', NULL, 0),
