(950071, 106707, 7743, '<td valign="top">I was guessing this was sunrise.  It just goes to show I don''t generally read titles.  Wonderful job and congrats on 1st place.</td>', 'I was guessing this was sunrise.  It just goes to show I don''t generally read titles.  Wonderful job and congrats on 1st place.', '2004-10-08 07:32:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(950075, 108872, 19982, '<td valign="top">This photo, for some reason, really turned me on.  I didn''t know how well it would place, but I handed out an extra 10 on this one hoping to see it score well.  Congratulations!  And thanks for showing us that even the simple things in life can be beautiful.<br/></td>', 'This photo, for some reason, really turned me on.  I didn''t know how well it would place, but I handed out an extra 10 on this one hoping to see it score well.  Congratulations!  And thanks for showing us that even the simple things in life can be beautiful.', '2004-10-08 07:36:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(950076, 108122, 17033, '<td valign="top">Little disappointed to see this place so low as I thought it would ribbon for sure. Having skimmed through the comments I am struck by the fact that what one person cites as a plus, another specifically criticises. I guess portraiture is a ''risky'' business because we all bring our own interpretation of human attractiveness to the table. I, for one, think your style gets the right balance between engaging with the subject but also remaining sufficiently objective so that the resulting photo doesn''t drip cloying sentimentality. Heida achieved a similar quality with her shot this challenge. Keep up the good work. Ben<br/>P.S. Will study your PS process in detail!</td>', 'Little disappointed to see this place so low as I thought it would ribbon for sure. Having skimmed through the comments I am struck by the fact that what one person cites as a plus, another specifically criticises. I guess portraiture is a ''risky'' business because we all bring our own interpretation of human attractiveness to the table. I, for one, think your style gets the right balance between engaging with the subject but also remaining sufficiently objective so that the resulting photo doesn''t drip cloying sentimentality. Heida achieved a similar quality with her shot this challenge. Keep up the good work. BenP.S. Will study your PS process in detail!', '2004-10-08 07:38:33.000000', NULL, 0),
