(950216, 108995, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nazgul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by timj351:</b></div><hr/><i> I screwed up on the title and I know it is a bass. Thanks for all of the feedback, it is greatly appreciated.<br/> <br/>T </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That maybe true but I think its fair to say that its not pretty common to call someone that plays BASS GUITAR a Guitarist?<br/> <br/>what do I know... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No, they''re usually called bassist or "the bass player." But this was one of my favorites -- I wasn''t marking it down for the title or anything.</td>', 'Originally posted by Nazgul: Originally posted by timj351: I screwed up on the title and I know it is a bass. Thanks for all of the feedback, it is greatly appreciated. T   That maybe true but I think its fair to say that its not pretty common to call someone that plays BASS GUITAR a Guitarist? what do I know...  No, they''re usually called bassist or "the bass player." But this was one of my favorites -- I wasn''t marking it down for the title or anything.', '2004-10-08 11:03:21.000000', NULL, 0),
