(951417, 107202, 4564, '<td valign="top">You''re right, I was too harsh: I should have offered them a map too.<br/> <br/>Lori, you shouldn''t take my comment personally; you didn''t vote.  Had you voted a 4 and under, I''d tell you the same thing I told them.  But that is not the case.  You used your judgement and decided that your personal taste would compromise your ability to properly rate this image.  I call that being very professional and respectful.<br/> <br/>I thought my choice of words to those ignorant fools was quite polite actually, considering the 31 votes of 4s and under (almost 10% of the people who voted on this image!).  4 and under: meaning, UNDER average.  Don''t get me wrong: I don''t mind not being in the top 3 and I think there were terrific images in this challenge.  So my comment has nothing to do with my position in the challenge.  <br/> <br/>It''s just that I pity those lost souls and I thought they''d benefit from some sympathy.  Offering them a solution on how to stick their heads out of their own ass hole was, I thought, a nice gesture.  After all, who in their right mind would like to be in that position?  Some guidance was in order!  A flash light and batteries was the first thing I thought of...  Digging their way out was out of the question; way too messy and they could hurt themselves.  <br/> <br/>My two cents.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GoldBerry:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrJOnes:</b></div><hr/><i> To all who gave this shot a rating bellow average (4 and under), I invite you to purchase a flash light and a set of batteries in order to find your way out of the deep ass hole you are currently lost in.  Thank you. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Woah..come on now, that''s harsh.  Nobody here said anything nasty about you if they didn''t like your work. Without sounding too after-school-special, not everyone has to love your genre and you don''t have to love theirs.  Because it isn''t my taste I would just not vote on it.  Should *I* being digging up some batteries?<br/> <br/>Thanks,<br/>Lori<br/> <br/>P.S. I''d skip voting on it because my personal views shouldn''t effect the scores of your technically-great work. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-09 15:52:29.</i></td>', 'You''re right, I was too harsh: I should have offered them a map too. Lori, you shouldn''t take my comment personally; you didn''t vote.  Had you voted a 4 and under, I''d tell you the same thing I told them.  But that is not the case.  You used your judgement and decided that your personal taste would compromise your ability to properly rate this image.  I call that being very professional and respectful. I thought my choice of words to those ignorant fools was quite polite actually, considering the 31 votes of 4s and under (almost 10% of the people who voted on this image!).  4 and under: meaning, UNDER average.  Don''t get me wrong: I don''t mind not being in the top 3 and I think there were terrific images in this challenge.  So my comment has nothing to do with my position in the challenge.   It''s just that I pity those lost souls and I thought they''d benefit from some sympathy.  Offering them a solution on how to stick their heads out of their own ass hole was, I thought, a nice gesture.  After all, who in their right mind would like to be in that position?  Some guidance was in order!  A flash light and batteries was the first thing I thought of...  Digging their way out was out of the question; way too messy and they could hurt themselves.   My two cents. Originally posted by GoldBerry: Originally posted by DrJOnes: To all who gave this shot a rating bellow average (4 and under), I invite you to purchase a flash light and a set of batteries in order to find your way out of the deep ass hole you are currently lost in.  Thank you.   Woah..come on now, that''s harsh.  Nobody here said anything nasty about you if they didn''t like your work. Without sounding too after-school-special, not everyone has to love your genre and you don''t have to love theirs.  Because it isn''t my taste I would just not vote on it.  Should *I* being digging up some batteries? Thanks,Lori P.S. I''d skip voting on it because my personal views shouldn''t effect the scores of your technically-great work. ', '2004-10-09 01:54:54.000000', '2004-10-09 16:52:29.000000', 0),
