(951917, 109013, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BradP:</b></div><hr/><i> Challenge or not, I hope this will find it''s way into a print and on your wall or in a scrapbook. Better yet, 2 prints - one for each of the boys. These will be precious moments in years to come.<br/> <br/>Shots like this move me so much more than a pretty landscape shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Now that I look at this again, I think it might look just fine if you just crop that nasty pole out of there and make it a square crop.</td>', 'Originally posted by BradP: Challenge or not, I hope this will find it''s way into a print and on your wall or in a scrapbook. Better yet, 2 prints - one for each of the boys. These will be precious moments in years to come. Shots like this move me so much more than a pretty landscape shot.  Now that I look at this again, I think it might look just fine if you just crop that nasty pole out of there and make it a square crop.', '2004-10-09 15:26:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(952068, 107387, 772, '<td valign="top">I''m coming back to this photo again after thinking about it for a few more days... <br/> <br/>This photo is a good example of where some information to go with the photo is very supportive of what the viewer sees.  In my original comment on this shot, I made reference to the ''haunting'' sound this instrument creates.  After the challenge, when I read your description about it being taken at Ground Zero, it added an entire new level of impact to the image.  The haunting sound of the music, coupled with a place on the map where thousands of people died, creates an entirely differen theme.<br/> <br/>May I suggest that you change the title of this photo from "Interlude" to "Requiem"?  It''s just a thought, but you can tie this theme together even better with "Requiem" since a requiem is a musical composition in honor/memory of the deceased.  <br/> <br/></td>', 'I''m coming back to this photo again after thinking about it for a few more days...  This photo is a good example of where some information to go with the photo is very supportive of what the viewer sees.  In my original comment on this shot, I made reference to the ''haunting'' sound this instrument creates.  After the challenge, when I read your description about it being taken at Ground Zero, it added an entire new level of impact to the image.  The haunting sound of the music, coupled with a place on the map where thousands of people died, creates an entirely differen theme. May I suggest that you change the title of this photo from "Interlude" to "Requiem"?  It''s just a thought, but you can tie this theme together even better with "Requiem" since a requiem is a musical composition in honor/memory of the deceased.   ', '2004-10-09 17:55:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(952087, 107202, 25150, '<td valign="top">This is a perfect shot, and it''s too bad some people vote on taste instead of photographic merit. You are an AMAZING professional photographer, and you are a true lighting master. This shot is absolutely stunning, I''m proud to say I voted this a 10, and would have given it a 12 if I could. Keep up the great work, You are a true pro!<br/>E</td>', 'This is a perfect shot, and it''s too bad some people vote on taste instead of photographic merit. You are an AMAZING professional photographer, and you are a true lighting master. This shot is absolutely stunning, I''m proud to say I voted this a 10, and would have given it a 12 if I could. Keep up the great work, You are a true pro!E', '2004-10-09 18:03:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(952108, 108767, 21183, '<td valign="top">Thanks for sharing this image with me in the ''mist'' thread - you''ve managed to bring to life many of the words contained within the poem there.  Your capture of the mist between the trees on this photo is brilliant.  There is a lovely mood within the shot and your sky is a perfect complimentary colour.</td>', 'Thanks for sharing this image with me in the ''mist'' thread - you''ve managed to bring to life many of the words contained within the poem there.  Your capture of the mist between the trees on this photo is brilliant.  There is a lovely mood within the shot and your sky is a perfect complimentary colour.', '2004-10-09 18:29:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(952161, 107202, 9913, '<td valign="top">Man thats Egomanic to say that everyone that voted this 4 or lower has a serios problem.....<br/> <br/>Could it be that this shot is not perfect (or below avarege) like you seem to belive?<br/>Could it be that you yourself have your head up your ass?<br/>and last but not least could it be that some people are tired of people like you who prefer not to be anounymous like most of us when it comes to voting.... I mean you could just as well spray your name on the wall in the background on each photo you submit.....<br/> <br/>And if your such a pro what the hell are you doing here?</td>', 'Man thats Egomanic to say that everyone that voted this 4 or lower has a serios problem..... Could it be that this shot is not perfect (or below avarege) like you seem to belive?Could it be that you yourself have your head up your ass?and last but not least could it be that some people are tired of people like you who prefer not to be anounymous like most of us when it comes to voting.... I mean you could just as well spray your name on the wall in the background on each photo you submit..... And if your such a pro what the hell are you doing here?', '2004-10-09 19:43:51.000000', NULL, 0),
