(978850, 108832, 23394, '<td valign="top">among sunset shots, this one really stands out.  as you found, it takes a lot of patience, waiting for what you can''t control; thanks for sticking it out!  <br/> <br/>the only things i might suggest in the future would be a deeper f-stop and a slower shutter (maybe even enough to justify a tripod).  as you found out, it takes a fair amount of work to go beyond capturing "another boring sunset" shot.  the key is balancing light, textures, and lines, and you have done a great job with this one.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-29 06:49:50.</i></td>', 'among sunset shots, this one really stands out.  as you found, it takes a lot of patience, waiting for what you can''t control; thanks for sticking it out!   the only things i might suggest in the future would be a deeper f-stop and a slower shutter (maybe even enough to justify a tripod).  as you found out, it takes a fair amount of work to go beyond capturing "another boring sunset" shot.  the key is balancing light, textures, and lines, and you have done a great job with this one.', '2004-10-29 07:44:35.000000', '2004-10-29 07:49:50.000000', 0),
